    ],
    "what": "Same asymmetry as ARC-002, for the use-case layer. M1: check-architecture.js reads forbiddenNamespaces (Microsoft.AspNetCore and the persistence technology namespaces) for the core-model and use-case layers from capabilities/architecture/clean-architecture/MODULE.md:49-52, run by its post-tool-use hook. L1: check-architecture.mjs:90-104 rejects Microsoft.AspNetCore.App (also implied by the Web SDK) and its packages in inner roles (check.json:11-12) and EF Core packages in domain/use-case roles (persistence/ef-core/enforcement.json), run by post-change-checks. K1: facets/architecture-style.cjs:73-85 errors on the Web SDK, the ASP.NET Core shared framework or Microsoft.AspNetCore.* packages in Domain/Application, and facets/persistence-technology.cjs errors on EF Core packages there. M, L0 and K0 have no such check (searched every hook and script for AspNetCore/EntityFrameworkCore/framework-reference logic).",
    "counterexample": "Same task: the agent adds Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore to the Application project to call ToListAsync in a service. Static outcome: L1 (enforcement.json forbiddenInRoles) and K1 (persistence-technology.cjs) report an error, M1 flags the EF Core namespace; M, L0 and K0 report nothing. Live-host effect of the finding NOT_RUN.",
